      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you on the nuance thing but the scale of this is just different. we aren't talking about a slow shift, we're talking about ai being able to do almost any cognitive task. if the jobs just don't come back, then the 're-skilling' argument feels kind of like a pipe dream. \n\ncan you just lay out the actual strongest case for why UBI is the only way to prevent a total collapse of consumer spending and mass poverty? i need the heavy hitters for the pro-UBI side to make my point stick. maybe differentiate between the moral welfare won period work but",
